  48:../src/middleware/bacnet/demo/handler/s_router.c **** /** Initialize an npdu_data structure with given parameters and good defaults,
  49:../src/middleware/bacnet/demo/handler/s_router.c ****  * and add the Network Layer Message fields.
  50:../src/middleware/bacnet/demo/handler/s_router.c ****  * The name is a misnomer, as it doesn't do any actual encoding here.
  51:../src/middleware/bacnet/demo/handler/s_router.c ****  * @see npdu_encode_npdu_data for a simpler version to use when sending an
  52:../src/middleware/bacnet/demo/handler/s_router.c ****  *           APDU instead of a Network Layer Message.
  53:../src/middleware/bacnet/demo/handler/s_router.c ****  *
  54:../src/middleware/bacnet/demo/handler/s_router.c ****  * @param npdu_data [out] Returns a filled-out structure with information
  55:../src/middleware/bacnet/demo/handler/s_router.c ****  * 					 provided by the other arguments and good defaults.
  56:../src/middleware/bacnet/demo/handler/s_router.c ****  * @param network_message_type [in] The type of Network Layer Message.
  57:../src/middleware/bacnet/demo/handler/s_router.c ****  * @param data_expecting_reply [in] True if message should have a reply.
  58:../src/middleware/bacnet/demo/handler/s_router.c ****  * @param priority [in] One of the 4 priorities defined in section 6.2.2,
  59:../src/middleware/bacnet/demo/handler/s_router.c ****  *                      like B'11' = Life Safety message
  60:../src/middleware/bacnet/demo/handler/s_router.c ****  */
